# Build inputs and outputs. NEVER commit these -- ci/checks/00-no-binaries.sh
# rejects them too, because .gitignore alone is not enough: `git add -f` and
# explicit paths bypass it, and history cannot be un-fattened afterwards.
isos/
work/
out/
*.iso
*.sb
*.img

# Session working files. See ci/checks/10-no-dnc.sh.
*.DNC.md

# The application payloads are fetched and verified by build.sh, not committed.
recipes/available/notepadpp32.files/
recipes/available/notepadpp64.files/
# ...and so is the Bottles Flatpak installation, which is 3 GiB unpacked.
recipes/available/bottles.files/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor leftovers.
*~

# Engine scratch dirs. bundle.packages and friends mkdtemp(dir=dirname(work)), i.e. as a
# SIBLING of work/, and remove them in a finally -- so these only survive a SIGKILL or a
# failed rmtree. When they do they are root-owned and full of unsquashed rootfs, which is
# the last thing that should reach `git add -A`.
kitchen-pkg-*/
kitchen-irfs-*/
kitchen-bb-*/
kitchen-bf-*/
kitchen-bt-*/
kitchen-bs-*/
kitchen-esp-*/

# A personal boot host. The vendored slax-kitchen reads `boot-host.ini` from the root of the
# project that vendors it -- this repository -- before its own checkout (slax-kitchen
# 49a465f, #66). It names a machine and an account, so it is ignored here, and
# ci/checks/10-no-dnc.sh (copied from upstream) refuses one that is ever staged.
/boot-host.ini
